    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but if the \"historical analog\" test is the standard now, isn't it basically impossible to pass for any modern safety regulation? it feels like the Court basically closed the door on any meaningful gun control by making it about the 1700s. isn't that argument just a legal loophole to ignore modern reality?",
